  "article": {
    "headline": "Man City beaten by double from Aston Villa's Jackson",
    "story": "<p>MANCHESTER, England -- <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"94fd5d7e-35b1-9d52-c9f2-4a37259bea36\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=382\">Manchester City</a>'s perfect start to the <a data-league-guid=\"6949f3af-300c-35f1-beab-b95669eedd38\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/soccer/league/_/name/ENG.1\">Premier League</a> season ended Saturday with a 2-1 loss at <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"610557ff-e870-ea0e-a3b2-8244df325d22\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=362\">Aston Villa</a>.</p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"ed90b32c-f09c-302e-af63-852a1e2a9352\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/308524/nicolas-jackson\">Nicolas Jackson</a> scored both goals for Villa against Enzo Maresca's City, who were aiming for an eighth straight win in the league.</p>\n<p>It also extended Villa's outstanding recent run to six wins from seven games in all competitions.</p>\n<p>Jackson is up to seven goals for the season in all competitions. He fired the opener inside six minutes at Villa Park.</p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"63b48f6c-a73d-78e7-71b9-21edae6b0e31\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/253989/erling-haaland\">Erling Haaland</a> headed City level in the second half, but Jackson got his second and the winner with a first-time finish that squirmed under goalkeeper <a data-player-guid=\"bafc75bd-f245-c2e3-c93b-ccf9907022bf\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/217092/gianluigi-donnarumma\">Gianluigi Donnarumma</a>.</p>\n<p>City fell to a fourth defeat at Villa Park in as many seasons.</p>\n\n"
  },
